From b57fd4438bf9db9c48b6c9743e7bcdc53ad9aac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ihor Buhaiov <freedbrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:09:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: Fix nonrd IntraBC DV range regression

Kit note: upstream libaom commit b57fd4438b on main (2026-10-12), in no release
yet (not 3.15.2, not 3.15.3). Only its code change is carried; its test change
(test/encode_api_test.cc) does not apply to 3.15.2 and the kit builds libaom
without tests. Why the kit carries it: with real-time screen content at
cpu-used 10, libaom 3.15.x writes intra block copy vectors the decoder rejects
on frames wider than about 2300 px (every AV1 frame fails, the picture stops),
and reads past the end of its dv_costs table (ASan heap-buffer-overflow in
mv_cost, av1/encoder/mcomp.c:299). Drop this patch when the pinned libaom
release contains b57fd4438b.

Upstream message:

    rtc: Fix nonrd IntraBC DV range regression
    
    Regression from 4a527cabbb ("rtc: Implement intrabc for nonrd
    pickmode"). av1_search_intrabc_nonrd() sets the search limits to the
    tile bounds, which drops the MV range clamp from
    av1_make_default_fullpel_ms_params(). On frames wider or taller than
    2048 pixels the hash search can then return a DV of 2048 pixels or more.
    
    The DV cost lookup in mv_cost() indexes the dv_costs table with the
    difference to the reference DV. For such a DV the index is outside the
    table, which is a heap buffer overflow read. The cost then comes from
    whatever memory follows the table, so the output is not deterministic.
    If the far DV wins, the encoder writes a DV the decoder rejects as
    invalid, or asserts in av1_get_mv_class() when the difference to the
    reference DV needs more than MV_CLASS_10.
    
    Call av1_set_mv_search_range() after setting the tile bounds, as the rd
    IntraBC search does. Add tests with a far copy to the left, above and
    above right. The above right one is reported by ASan as a heap buffer
    overflow without the fix.
    
    Change-Id: I1cbd0ef09ab764e7424b679393985262ab7f4fbc
    
---
diff --git a/av1/encoder/nonrd_pickmode.c b/av1/encoder/nonrd_pickmode.c
index 7bf0a93fcb..0034f1292f 100644
--- a/av1/encoder/nonrd_pickmode.c
+++ b/av1/encoder/nonrd_pickmode.c
@@ -1647,6 +1647,7 @@ static void av1_search_intrabc_nonrd(AV1_COMP *cpi, MACROBLOCK *x,
   fullms_params.mv_limits.row_min = (xd->tile.mi_row_start - mi_row) * MI_SIZE;
   fullms_params.mv_limits.row_max =
       (xd->tile.mi_row_end - mi_row) * MI_SIZE - block_size_high[bsize];
+  av1_set_mv_search_range(&fullms_params.mv_limits, &dv_ref.as_mv);
   int_mv best_mv;
   int bestsme = INT_MAX;
   if (!cpi->sf.mv_sf.hash_max_8x8_intrabc_blocks || bsize <= BLOCK_8X8) {
